# HEM-7196T1-FLE (M4 Connect AFib): encrypted single-channel WLP Pair (Omron's WLP1COM_PAIR in registration mode,
# OpenPressure's X7_SECURE_WLP Pair): a fresh application pairing (70 01 / F0 81, 70 05 / F0 85, 70 06 / F0 86), the
# encrypted authorization poll, then Omron's pairing transfer for user 2 and OpenPressure's read-only import that the
# user starts after Pair. Experimental and hardware-untested in OpenPressure; the public HEM-7196T1-FLE capture shows
# only a saved-key reconnection, not a first pairing. Both clients select the encrypted route from the type-9
# advertisement with the pairing flag (category 0, model 0x00EB, two users). The fresh Android bond that precedes the
# session exchanges no GATT bytes and is not modelled. Steps after `secure` are plaintext; the cuff-side test peer
# decrypts and encrypts them (docs/omron-sandbox.md).
name hem-7196t1/pair-encrypted
flow pair
register user=2
advertise name=BLEsmart_000000EB0011223344 services=0000fe4a-0000-1000-8000-00805f9b34fb msd=0e020909000000eb0001000100
# Synthetic Device Information. The model string a physical HEM-7196T1-FLE reports is unknown; OpenPressure accepts
# only the exact model number. Omron reads the serial number on this model, OpenPressure only the model.
dis model=HEM-7196T1-FLE serial=0000000001 firmware=0001 software=0001 systemid=0011223344556677
time 2026-01-02T03:04:05 zone=UTC
# Required by the format; a fresh pairing derives its own application key, which both clients keep afterwards.
key 05050505050505050505050505050505
mtu 247

alias tx db5b55e0-aee7-11e1-965e-0002a5d5c51b
alias rx 49123040-aee8-11e1-a74d-0002a5d5c51b
alias sys b305b680-aee7-11e1-a730-0002a5d5c51b

# One synthetic record per user (60-slot banks: user 2 at 0x584), each with sequence number 1 at offset 10 and the
# 8-bit sum of bytes 0-13 at offset 14: user 1 130/78 mmHg, pulse 67, 2025-07-09 06:14:38; user 2 120/80 mmHg, pulse 70,
# 2025-08-01 07:30:00 with AFib (irregular pulse and movement masked for this model). Omron's Pair does not read them;
# OpenPressure's import after Pair does.
memory fill=ff
memory 0x1c4 694e4319 261d a603 0000 0100 00000000
memory 0x584 5f504619 27e0 8027 0000 0100 0000 bd00
# Index (index_setting_read_address=10): per user next write position 1, one unsent record and sequence number 1;
# empty error-log and pulse-wave pointers.
memory 0x10 0100 0100 0100 0100 01000000 01000000 000000000000 0000
# Setting-information block 3 at 0x3c: only user 1 registered (byte 48 = 01), clock 2026-01-02 03:04:05, additive
# checksum of bytes 44-57 at byte 58. Block 4 at 0x4c is zero.
memory 0x3c 00000000 01000000 1a0102030405 2a00
memory 0x4c 0000000000000000

nonce sys
# Fresh application pairing; the cuff peer derives the same LTK as the phone.
secure sys fresh reserved=aabbccddeeff00000000000000000000
# Encrypted authorization poll on SYS; the cuff reports COMPLETE (01) at once.
write sys 20 01 00 00000000000000000000000000000000 00
notify sys a0 01 00 01 00000000000000000000000000000000

write tx 08 00 00 00 00 10 00 18
notify rx 08 80 00 00 00 10 00 98

[omron-only: Omron reads the index (index_setting_pointer_unsend_size 24 plus setting-information blocks 1 and 2) in one frame] reads 0x10 44 chunk=44
[omron-only: Omron reads setting-information blocks 3 and 4 at 0x3c in one frame; pairing flags 0x1210 then return settings without reading history] reads 0x3c 24 chunk=24
[ours-only: after an encrypted Pair, which never registers, the user starts Import: the 68-byte settings/index image at 0x10 in 16-byte blocks, then the populated slots] reads 0x10 68 chunk=16
[ours-only: import after Pair, user 1's populated slot] reads 0x1c4 16 chunk=16
[ours-only: import after Pair, user 2's populated slot at 0x584 on this 60-slot map] reads 0x584 16 chunk=16

[omron-only: Omron 2026.09.03 Pair user 2, index prefix at 0x54 with user 2's unsent counter cleared to 0x8000 and its error-log unsent count (offset 19) to 0x80; docs/omron-sandbox.md] write tx 2001c0005418 010001000100008001000000010000000000008000000000 00ac
[omron-only: synthetic full echo acknowledgment; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 2081c0005418 010001000100008001000000010000000000008000000000 002c
[omron-only: Omron 2026.09.03 Pair user 2, birthday block 2 (default 1900-01-01) merged with block 3 at 0x76 (user-2 bit, clock + 1 s, checksum 2d); docs/omron-sandbox.md] write tx 2201c000761a 000101fffffffffffdff 00000000030000001a01020304062d00 0044
[omron-only: synthetic full echo acknowledgment; the physical monitor reply is unconfirmed] notify rx 2281c000761a 000101fffffffffffdff 00000000030000001a01020304062d00 00c4

write tx 08 0f 00 00 00 00 00 07
notify rx 08 8f 00 00 00 00 00 87

[ours-only: OpenPressure's import after Pair; Omron's pairing flags 0x1210 read no history] expect reading user=1 sys=130 dia=78 pulse=67 time=2025-07-09T06:14:38 irregular=0 movement=0 afib=0
[ours-only: OpenPressure's import after Pair; Omron's pairing flags 0x1210 read no history] expect reading user=2 sys=120 dia=80 pulse=70 time=2025-08-01T07:30:00 irregular=0 movement=0 afib=1
